Subject: [PATCH] cpuset: match the allow_attach() signature

cgroup calls ss->allow_attach(css, tset) (include/linux/cgroup-defs.h), but cpuset_allow_attach()
took only tset, so it read the css pointer as the task set. clang 23 rejects the initializer
(-Wincompatible-function-pointer-types). Take both arguments; dst_css is unused, as before.

diff --git a/kernel/cpuset.c b/kernel/cpuset.c
index a045358a..76f4a587 100644
--- a/kernel/cpuset.c
+++ b/kernel/cpuset.c
@@ -2145,7 +2145,7 @@ void cpuset_fork(struct task_struct *task)
 	task->mems_allowed = current->mems_allowed;
 }
 
-static int cpuset_allow_attach(struct cgroup_taskset *tset)
+static int cpuset_allow_attach(struct cgroup_subsys_state *dst_css, struct cgroup_taskset *tset)
 {
 	const struct cred *cred = current_cred(), *tcred;
 	struct task_struct *task;
